---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Quote Request
heading: Quote Request
standfirst: Tell us what you need and we'll come back to you with a clear price. Not sure how to describe it? Just ask for a callback.
description: Request a quote or a callback from IT Surgery — friendly IT help for homes and small businesses in Penarth, Barry and Cardiff. No obligation.
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="lead">
      Please complete the form with as much information as you can. We are happy
      to quote for any task or project. If you are not sure how to describe what
      you need, simply ask for a callback and we will phone you to talk it
      through, then provide a quote.
    </p>

    <p class="contact-alt">
      Rather not fill in a form?
      <a href="https://wa.me/{{ site.whatsapp }}?text=Hello%2C%20I%27d%20like%20some%20help%20with%20an%20IT%20problem" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Message us on WhatsApp<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
      — you can even send a photo of the error message — or email
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.
      You can also call <a href="tel:{{ site.phoneLink }}">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a>;
      if we are out on a job, leave a message or drop us a WhatsApp and we will
      come back to you.
    </p>

    {# Handled by Netlify Forms — no server or backend needed. #}
    <div class="form-wrap">
      <h2>Request a quote or callback</h2>
      {#
        Netlify Forms. Two things are required for this to work:
        1. "Enable form detection" must be turned on in the Netlify UI
           (Forms > Usage and configuration). It is opt-in. Without it Netlify
           never registers the form and the POST returns a 404.
        2. This form must be present in the built static HTML, which it is.
        When detection is working, Netlify strips data-netlify from the
        deployed markup and injects a hidden form-name input — that is how you
        can tell from the page source whether it is switched on.
      #}
      <form name="quote" method="POST" action="/thanks/" data-netlify="true" data-netlify-honeypot="bot-field">
        {# Honeypot. Off-screen rather than display:none, because some bots skip
           hidden fields. aria-hidden and tabindex="-1" keep it out of the tab order
           and the accessibility tree — without them a keyboard user tabs into an
           invisible box and loses focus off-screen. #}
        <p class="hidden-field" aria-hidden="true">
          <label>Don't fill this in if you're human: <input name="bot-field" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label>
        </p>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="name">Your name</label>
          <input id="name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required />
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="phone">Phone number</label>
          <input id="phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" required />
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="email">Email <span class="optional">(optional)</span></label>
          <input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" />
        </div>

        <fieldset class="field">
          <legend>What do you need help with?</legend>
          <label class="radio"><input type="radio" name="type" value="personal" checked /> Home / personal IT</label>
          <label class="radio"><input type="radio" name="type" value="business" /> Business IT</label>
        </fieldset>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="problem">How can we help?</label>
          <textarea id="problem" name="problem" rows="5"
            placeholder="A sentence or two is plenty — for example: my laptop has become very slow."></textarea>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="when">Best time to call you <span class="optional">(optional)</span></label>
          <input id="when" name="when" type="text" placeholder="e.g. weekday mornings" />
        </div>

        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Send request</button>
        <p class="form-note">
          We'll only use your details to get back to you about your enquiry.
        </p>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="booking-placeholder">
      <p><strong>Prefer to pick your own slot?</strong></p>
      <p>Online booking is coming shortly.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
